        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1cca3578-7fb9-5848-96ba-f05daa6019ce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jameel Sayhood, Craig Underhill, Cesar Rodriguez\n- Products: MiG-29B, McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle, F-15C\n- Organizations: Iraqi Air Force, USAF, McDonnell Douglas, Boeing\n- Events: Gulf War, aerial combat\n- Concepts: air supremacy, aerial victory\n\nFacts:\n- During the Gulf War, Captain Jameel Sayhood was an Iraqi pilot.\n- It is claimed that during the Gulf War, Jameel Sayhood achieved one of the few aerial victories credited to the Iraqi Air Force while flying a MiG-29B.\n- Minutes after that claimed air-air victory, USAF Captains Craig Underhill and Cesar Rodriguez shot down Jameel Sayhood in their F-15Cs.\n- The McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle is an American twin-engine, all-weather tactical fighter aircraft.\n- McDonnell Douglas designed the F-15 Eagle to gain and maintain air supremacy in aerial combat.\n- McDonnell Douglas is now part of Boeing.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
